  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 504 PM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThe cold front has moved through our area with lingering snow\nshowers over our eastern areas. The heavier of these showers \nlook to continue until around 5 am, when the winter weather \nadvisories for the eastern mountains expire. Expect lingering \nlight snow showers for our extreme northeastern areas (Island\nPark/Driggs) until late tomorrow morning. Tomorrow afternoon \nwill be cold, with most areas below 40 degrees. Tonight, a \ntrough behind the cold front will bring breezy to moderate winds\novernight with gusts of 20 to 40 mph likely. Winds will drop \noff by mid to late tomorrow morning. Lower clouds will lift by \nmid to late tomorrow morning for all areas.  Meanwhile, mid to \nupper level clouds start moving in from our west by tomorrow\nafternoon ahead of the next system. \n\nThis next system will start moving through late tomorrow \nevening into Thursday morning and continue for eastern areas \nthrough Saturday morning. Thursday through Saturday morning \nexpect 4 to 12 inches of snow for the Sun Valley region and Big \nLost Highlands, where a winter weather advisory will likely be \nneeded. Mountains elsewhere will get 3 to 8 inches, including \nthe Central mountains, Montana Divide, Southern Highlands, and \nthe Eastern Highlands. Lower elevations will likely see a trace \nto 1 inch of snow. However, there is some uncertainty with snow \nlevels. Snow levels could drop more than currently forecast and \nup to 2 inches of snow is possible currently for lower \nelevations. There is about a 50 to 70% chance of Burley, \nPocatello, and Idaho Falls to get 1 inch of snow with this next \nsystem. \n\nSaturday and Sunday appear mostly dry with a brief break before\nanother shortwave trough arrives late Sunday from the west \ncoast. This trough will bring wet conditions late Sunday into \nMonday. However, temperatures will be slightly warmer with west \nto southwest winds allowing some locations to exceed the 40 deg \nF threshold, especially on Sunday.",
